# Mechanical artifacts in extracted phonetics

## ==Original Issue==

Some extracted phonetics contain obvious mechanical junk: embedded HTML
comments, stray quote characters, truncation against source breaks, and
literal-prose fragments instead of phonetics. These are the most deterministic
of the five classes and should be cleaned by character-level rules.

### Concrete examples

- `Melbourne`             -> phonetic contains a raw `<!-- ... -->` HTML comment
- `Bangladesh`            -> stray `"` quote character in the phonetic
- `Osprey`                -> stray `"` quote character
- `Donetsk`               -> truncated (`dən`)
- `Eigenvalues & eigen-vec…` -> truncated (`eigen-`), plus full-width ellipsis
- `Guelphs and Ghibellines` -> phonetic contains a literal `…` (ellipsis) instead of "and"

## ==Status Report: 2026-10-24 18:10 US/Pacific==

Implemented the deterministic pieces:

1. `normalize_ipac_en` / `normalize_respell` strip inline HTML comments
   (`<!-- ... -->`) from param values via a shared `_strip_comment` helper.
2. `_ipac_table.py` gained `'"': 'ˈ'` so the legacy double-quote primary-stress
   code is mapped (it was leaking through literally as a stray quote).
3. `normalize_respell` rstrip handles dangling `-`/`_`.

Live-verified: Melbourne -> `MEL-bərn` (comment gone), Bangladesh ->
`ˌbæŋɡləˈdɛʃ` (no stray quote), Osprey -> `ˈɒspri`. Added
`test_respell_html_comment_is_stripped` and
`test_ipac_en_legacy_double_quote_is_primary_stress`. Suite: 174 passed.

NOT fixed (left for human review, out of mechanical scope): the `...` ellipsis
in multi-name titles (e.g. "Guelphs and Ghibellines") and dangling `-` forms
that are really *partial-name* transcriptions (e.g. "Eigenvalues…" -> "EYE-gən",
"Donetsk" -> "dən") — those belong to ticket 06 (partial names), not to
mechanical cleanup.